.TH AVR\-API 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-api \- Call an Avrea API endpoint.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr api
[OPTIONS] <endpoint>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Call an Avrea API endpoint.
.PP
Use GET by default, or POST when supplying fields or input. With GET, HEAD, or --input, fields become query parameters.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
  avr api users/me/organizations
  avr api /orgs/acme/workflow-runs -X GET -F limit=5
  avr api /logs/search --input search.json
  avr api users/me/organizations -i
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIENDPOINT\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-field\fR, \fB\-F\fR \fITEXT\fR
Add a typed field (key=value, @file or @-). (default: (); repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-header\fR, \fB\-H\fR \fITEXT\fR
Set a request header (name: value). (default: (); repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-include\fR, \fB\-i\fR
Print response status and headers.
.TP
\fB\-\-input\fR \fITEXT\fR
Read the body from a file or - for stdin.
.TP
\fB\-\-jq\fR, \fB\-q\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter the JSON response.
.TP
\fB\-\-method\fR, \fB\-X\fR \fITEXT\fR
HTTP request method.
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\-field\fR, \fB\-f\fR \fITEXT\fR
Add a literal string field (key=value). (default: (); repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-silent\fR
Suppress the response body.
